Fork patch: let the n-gram chain's propose() override carry intermediate_tensors.

dflash2-ngram-chains.patch (upstream #38) adds a propose() override on
DFlash2Speculator that delegates to super().propose(). Its signature is a copy
of stock 0.27.1's, which has no intermediate_tensors parameter -- but this
fork's zz-dflash2-pipeline-parallel.patch adds exactly that parameter to the
base DFlashSpeculator.propose(), because under pipeline parallelism the
speculator runs on the last rank and needs the hidden states the previous stage
sent. The model runner passes it by keyword on every step, so the override
shadows the base method and the engine dies during warmup, before the first
token:

  File "vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py", line 1638, in sample_tokens
    draft_tokens = self.speculator.propose(
  TypeError: DFlash2Speculator.propose() got an unexpected keyword argument
  'intermediate_tensors'

Reproduced on this pair with heterogeneous/start_qwen_dflash2_solo.sh: pool
sizes correctly at 202,174 tokens, both ranks capture their graphs, and
Worker_PP1 then raises the TypeError in warmup_kernels. It fires with
VLLM_DFLASH2_CHAIN unset as well as set -- the mismatch is in the signature,
not in the chain logic -- so on this fork the upstream patch takes out BOTH
DFlash2 profiles rather than only the opt-in feature.

The fix is to accept the parameter and forward it. The chain fast path does not
need it: _chain_generate never runs the draft model forward (context KV insert
+ suffix lookup + point-mass rewrite only), so there are no cross-stage hidden
states for it to consume. Only the super() delegation carries it through.

Named zzzz- so it applies after both dflash2-ngram-chains.patch (which creates
the override) and zz-dflash2-pipeline-parallel.patch (which creates the reason
it needs fixing).

--- a/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/dflash2/speculator.py
+++ b/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/dflash2/speculator.py
@@ -418,6 +418,7 @@
         skip_attn_for_dummy_run=False,
         mm_inputs=None,
         is_profile=False,
+        intermediate_tensors=None,
     ):
         # Chain eligibility is decided HERE, on the host, once per step --
         # propose() is never captured, so this state machine survives FULL
@@ -495,6 +496,7 @@
             skip_attn_for_dummy_run=skip_attn_for_dummy_run,
             mm_inputs=mm_inputs,
             is_profile=is_profile,
+            intermediate_tensors=intermediate_tensors,
         )
 
     def _chain_should_engage(self, prev_missed: bool) -> bool:
